			"notes": "- Added the Construction Cannon\n  - Shift right click to open the gui\n  - Select a material, construct, and placement settings\n  - Any survival-obtainable block in a material's set can be used as input for the cannon\n- Added building blocks\n  - There's about 300, including slabs/stairs/walls/facades!\n- Added Pedestal Buttons\n  - Right click a pedestal button with a hammer to open the gui\n  - Press time, offset, and whether or not the button should have an additional baseplate can all be changed\n- Added Floor Buttons\n  - Now are proper multiblocks\n  - Can be pressed by any entity that can press a stone pressure plate\n    - Cube buttons can only be pressed by cubes, of course\n- Added Props\n  - Grabbed with G, and rebindable from the keybinds menu\n  - Whether or not another player can snatch the prop you're holding is now controlled by a gamerule, defaulting to true\n- Added Magnesium\n  - A new ore used for Portal Cubed crafting\n  - Generates from y=32 to y=-16 with roughly the same abundancy as Iron\n  - Can be used as an armor trim material and beacon base block\n\nSome other notes about the alpha:\n- Portal Cubed is now on 1.20.4\n- There's no Portal Gun/Portals yet.  They're simply not finished yet, and will be part of Alpha 2.\n- While just about everything *does* have a recipe, it isn't recommended to use this version in survival.  Many of them are placeholders/not final.\n- **OLD MAPS ARE NOT COMPATIBLE**.  If you try and load a world from pre-rewrite versions, you **will** lose blocks.  We know people have put a lot of effort into custom maps using Portal Cubed, so in the future I plan on making a datapack to help convert the blocks in old worlds to the new IDs in the rewrite."
